WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 3:
Clothing, Fashion, and Sustainability.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.120
Welcome to Unit 3.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.760
This unit explores the world of
clothing, fashion, and sustainability.

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.980
You will learn about how clothes are made,
why the choices we make as consumers matter,

5
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:23.040
and what people around the world are doing to
protect the environment through sustainable fashion.

6
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.860
You will also build your skills in
multi-word verbs (phrasal verbs like "put on",

7
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.860
"dress up" and "turn off") and learn how to use
the passive voice to describe processes and actions.

8
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.360
Alongside the topic work, you will
read the story "A Voice in the Valley",

9
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:47.900
about a quiet girl named Hannah in rural Ethiopia who
discovers that her writing can inspire an entire community.

10
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:55.160
By the end of the unit, you will write an eco-project
report, give a short speech about sustainable fashion, and...

11
00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.480
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

12
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:07.460
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use
vocabulary related to clothing, materials, fast fashion,

13
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.580
and the environment.

14
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:16.480
you will also understand and use multi-word verbs (phrasal
verbs) such as put on, take off, dress up, throw away,

15
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.300
and give away.

16
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:25.440
you will also form sentences in the present passive ("cotton
is grown in many countries") and past passive ("the dress

17
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.560
was made by hand").

18
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.100
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:37.680
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: alliteration,
rhyme, rhythm, repetition, punctuation, figurative.

20
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.620
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

21
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.300
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

22
00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:54.980
The reading sequence includes Clothing, Fashion, and
Sustainability: source text 1 and Clothing, Fashion,

23
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.000
and Sustainability: source text 2.

24
00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.480
Read actively.

25
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.360
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

26
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.260
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

27
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.960
The first language focus is Multi-Word Verbs.

28
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:20.820
What the rule means and why it matters Multi-word verbs
(also called phrasal verbs) are special combinations of a main

29
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.460
verb and one or more particles (small words like on,

30
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.300
off, up, down, away, out).

31
00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:32.500
Together, these words create a new meaning that is
often different from the meaning of the verb alone.

32
00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:38.960
For example, "put" means to place something,
but "put on" means to wear something.

33
00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:46.020
Multi-word verbs are extremely common in everyday
English, and knowing them will help you communicate more...

34
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:52.840
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

35
00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.440
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

36
00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.320
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

37
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.980
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

38
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.620
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

39
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.440
You are ready to begin.

40
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.940
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

41
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.700
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

42
00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:27.660
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
